      "rationale": "Excellent axis for the query: whether the class delivered value directly speaks to value-for-money and recommendation. Most samples sound (premium_underdelivered, economy_exceeded_expectations), but 'value_met' assigned to a very short positive economy note is a stretch, and the label requires class context not always present, slightly weakening groundedness."
    },
    {
      "name": "service_consistency_decline",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Boolean capturing perceived decline/inconsistency is relevant to the improvement query, though it partially overlaps with the crew-quality axis. Sampled 'False' values match texts that report consistent good service."
    },
    {
      "name": "loyalty_program_friction",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.5,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A niche boolean (33 true) about loyalty/status friction; only marginally connected to the general rating/recommendation query and near-constant. Sampled 'False' values are correctly assigned where no loyalty program is mentioned."
