  "analytical_usefulness": 0.82,
  "source_groundedness": 0.85,
  "rationale": "The added columns collectively provide several genuinely useful analytical axes (crew service quality, food issue types, class value gap, amenity reduction) that map well onto diagnosing why passengers do not recommend the airline and where improvement is possible. A couple of columns (special_meal_service_failure, loyalty_program_friction) are narrow near-constant booleans with limited leverage. Groundedness is generally solid, with sampled values reading soundly from source text; the main weaknesses are over-confident inferences on silent rows for crew quality (labeling a seat-only complaint as 'inattentive_robotic') and class-value labels where class context is thin."
